#gpseudo repaint the note and marks when only the step changes
#gpseudo mark and scroll to the first marked line after each diff fill
#gstep careful Draw the steps in the left pane
#gwhy The guide pane replaces the changed-file list: ticks, folds, pseudocode and each step's files with the current one highlighted. The header also tells when a guide could not be read.
#ghunk src/renderer/lib/lanternguideview.ts
#ghunk src/renderer/lib/lanternprpanel.ts
#gpseudo draw summary, risk and one card per step with its files
#gpseudo highlight the current file under its own step
#gpseudo keep ticks and folds per pull request
#gstep careful Wire the review screen to the guide
#gwhy The view swaps the file list for the guide pane, builds the review target and stepping from the stops, and drops the Guide view. Macro keeps the plain list and order.
#ghunk src/renderer/lib/lanternview.ts
#gpseudo when the pull request has a guide and Macro is off, use the guide stops for the file order
#gpseudo a click on a guide file opens it as a diff at that step and keeps focus there
#gpseudo arrow stepping moves to the next stop and resolves its step
#gstep skim Drop the Guide switch and restyle
#gwhy The strip goes back to Files, Macro and Flow, and the styles move from the full-screen view to the left pane, the note and the marked lines.
